OL,0,          BTXT64  GFri 27.11.26 06:06:50
OL,1,T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,2,FTeletextC64D]FMeatloaf                 
OL,3,   EUltimateD]GRead all about it        
OL,4,T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,5, into the IEC serial port of a Commodore
OL,6, 64, 128, VIC-20 or Plus/4 andFpretends 
OL,7,Fto be a disk driveG- but one whose     
OL,8, "diskettes" can live on flash, on SD   
OL,9, card, or on any server on the Internet.
OL,11, -BIt is a disk drive.GLOAD"$",8 works. 
OL,12,   LOAD"*",8 works. Your existing       
OL,13,   software does not know the difference
OL,15, -BIts disks can be anywhere.GA D64 on  
OL,16,   your NAS, a ZIP on a web server, a   
OL,17,   tape image on an FTP site - all      
OL,18,   addressed as ordinary filenames.     
OL,20, -BIt is 26 drives at once.GConfigure it
OL,21,   to answer on any device IDs from 4 to
OL,22,   30 simultaneously, each with its own 
OL,23,D]F307G<<                >>F312 B]D2/4  
OL,24,AMain page  BA-Z Index  CInstall  FAbout
FL,100,199,200,300,0,100
